# Trivy's baseline for the image scan in .github/workflows/ci.yml (the
# `docker` job scans every image before it is pushed and fails on a
# fixable HIGH or CRITICAL). These are the advisories that were already
# open against the production dependencies when the gate went in — the
# same list pnpm-workspace.yaml's auditConfig.ignoreGhsas carries for
# `pnpm audit`, by the id Trivy reports (the CVE where one exists, the
# GHSA otherwise). Each line expires: past its date Trivy counts the
# finding again and the push fails, so fix the dependency and delete the
# line, or renew the date with a reason. Keep the two lists in step.

# image-size 1.2.1 under pptxgenjs
CVE-2025-71329 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2025-71330 exp:2026-11-30

# jsoup 1.19.1 under the Eclipse JDT language server in the sandbox image
# (usr/local/jdtls/plugins/org.jsoup_1.19.1.jar; CVE-2026-75140, denial of
# service via deeply nested XML). jdtls 1.61.0 is the latest milestone and
# bundles it; the 1.62.0 snapshots already carry jsoup 1.23.2, so the next
# milestone lifts this line (bump JDTLS_VERSION in docker/Dockerfile and
# delete it). Snapshots are pruned from download.eclipse.org, so one is not
# pinned. Not a pnpm dependency, so no auditConfig counterpart.
CVE-2026-75140 exp:2026-11-30
